      "text": "```\n+----------------------------------------------------------+\n|  PHONETICS                    PHONOLOGY                  |\n|  (physical facts of sound)    (abstract sound systems)   |\n|                                                          |\n|  Articulatory:                 Phonemes:                 |\n|  where/how vocal tract         the distinctive units     |\n|  produces sounds               (not physical sounds)     |\n|                                                          |\n|  Acoustic:                     Allophony:                |\n|  waveforms, spectrograms,      predictable variants      |\n|  formants, F0                  of a phoneme              |\n|                                                          |\n|  Auditory:                     Phonological rules:       |\n|  how cochlea/auditory          how phonemes combine,     |\n|  cortex processes sound        change in context         |\n|                                                          |\n|  Studies physical signal       Studies the grammar of    |\n|  and its production            sound — the abstract      |\n|                                system speakers know      |\n+----------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
